Mitcad patch (mitcad#343): the tolerance of the point where an OnSame end's
cap leaves the prolongation tangentially takes in their crossings near it.

A thread cut as a groove, its crest's edges rounded up to the groove's
floor (a plane square to the axis): each rounding ends where its contact on
the crest's cylinder meets the floor, the floor's edge with the cylinder
prolonged up to there, and the floor cuts the rounding along a cap that
leaves that circle tangentially and runs inside it, a few micrometres from
it for a while (both run round the axis). The cap's approximation passed
over to the circle's side there and crossed it 0.053 from their common
point, whose tolerance was 5e-5, the circle's 1e-7: the floor's wire was
self-intersecting (BRepCheck). Where the cap and the prolongation meet
tangentially at that point (within a hundredth of a radian), their
crossings within a hundredth of the cap's length from it are added to the
box the point's tolerance is made from (ChFi3d_TangentCapCrossings).

